Subject: text-reveal: widths come from a ResizeObserver

What: TextReveal records its entering and leaving widths from a ResizeObserver and widens
its track from there, instead of reading scrollWidth at mount, on every growth of the
text and again after fonts load. The track interpolates only numeric widths.
Why: each scrollWidth read forced a synchronous layout of whatever the page had dirtied,
which on a session switch was the whole incoming transcript (16-17 ms per switch in a
mid-stream trace). Under an inherited interpolate-size: allow-keywords the first
measured width would otherwise animate from auto.

diff --git a/src/components/text-reveal.css b/src/components/text-reveal.css
index 80e12168bb..f236bab3a3 100644
--- a/src/components/text-reveal.css
+++ b/src/components/text-reveal.css
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@
     justify-items: start;
     align-items: center;
     overflow: visible;
+    /* The width starts as auto and the first measurement lands after mount, when
+       transitions may already be on; under an inherited interpolate-size: allow-keywords
+       that first auto-to-px change would animate for the whole duration. */
+    interpolate-size: numeric-only;
     transition: width var(--_dur) var(--_spring-soft);
   }
 
